      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2012 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "A novel class of 1,7-disubstituted 2,3,4,5-tetrahydro-1H-benzo[b]azepine derivatives was designed, synthesized and evaluated as human nitric oxide synthase (NOS) inhibitors. Structure-activity relationship studies based on various basic amine side chains attached at the 1-position of the 2,3,4,5-tetrahydro-1H-benzo[b]azepine ring led to the identification of several potent and highly selective inhibitors (17, 18, 25, (±)-39, and (±)-40) of human neuronal NOS. The potential therapeutic application of one of these new selective nNOS inhibitors (17) was demonstrated in an in vivo spinal nerve ligation model of neuropathic pain, and various in vitro safety pharmacology studies such as the hERG K(+) channel inhibition assay and high throughput broad screen (minimal activity at 79 receptors/transporters/ion channels)."
      },
